## Argument Reference

- `template_id` (Required, Forces replacement) — WAF template ID.
- `configs` (Required) — Typed {{.Resource.OperationName}} configuration. Its attributes and ownership-wrapper blocks are identical to `fortiappseccloud_{{.Resource.TypeNameSuffix}}` when that app resource uses `template = false`.

## Import

Import using the template ID:

```shell
terraform import fortiappseccloud_waf_template_{{.Resource.TypeNameSuffix | trimWAFPrefix}}.example TEMPLATE_ID
```

The first read after import hydrates all supported ownership wrappers.

## Destroy Behavior

{{- if .Resource.TemplateDestroyDisables}}
{{- if .Resource.TemplateDestroyCoupledFields}}
Destroy performs a fresh GET, preserves the complete response, sets `template=false`, `configs.status=false`, `configs.cache.status=false`, and `configs.compress.status=false`, sends the complete PUT, and verifies the normalized GET response before Terraform removes the resource from state. The three statuses are a reviewed coupled disable contract for template caching/compression.
{{- else}}
Destroy performs a fresh GET, preserves the complete response, sets `template=false` and `configs.status=false`, sends the complete PUT, and verifies the normalized GET response before Terraform removes the resource from state.
{{- end}}
{{- else}}
Destroy forgets this resource without sending a disabling PUT. The remote {{.Resource.OperationName}} template configuration remains unchanged and Terraform emits a warning.
{{- end}}
